3. LIST OUTPUT INCLUDES THE FIELD, WITHOUT omitempty SO false SERIALIZES
   — PASS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Asserted on the SERIALIZED JSON, not on the struct tag, because "false must
render" is a claim about output bytes:
  $ go test -overlay=<probe> -count=1 -v -run TestProbeListRowSerializesFalse ./internal/services/mcpsvc/curate/
    PROBE-ROW marshal(zero value) = {"id":"x","name":"n","keywords":null,"expected_min":0,"expected_max":0,"is_internal_transfer":false,"exclude_from_plan_sync":false,"count":0,"pinned_count":0,"total":0}
    PROBE-ROW contains exclude_from_plan_sync:false = true
    PROBE-ROW marshal(true) contains :true = true
The zero-value row emits `"exclude_from_plan_sync":false` — it is NOT
suppressed. Tag is `json:"exclude_from_plan_sync"` with no omitempty, matching
`is_internal_transfer` in the same struct (visible side by side in the marshal
output above). Populated in the row-building loop from `e.ExcludeFromPlanSync`
(expenses.go:113). Note this struct is shared: majorExpenseRow is also
upsertOutput.Expense, so the upsert response inherits the same non-suppressing
behaviour.

